# =============================================================================
# ifupdown-ng -- interface configuration database (interfaces)
# =============================================================================
# What this is: the interface configuration database read by ifup(8) /
# ifdown(8) (AUR package `ifupdown-ng`). ELI5: the wiring diagram -- which
# plugs (interfaces) get turned on automatically and how each one gets its
# address.
# Syntax notes: `auto <iface>` brings the interface up at boot;
# `iface <iface>` starts a definition stanza; `use <executor>` picks the
# tool that configures it (dhcp, static, ipv6-ra, bond, bridge, ...);
# executors run in the order of their `use` statements and may also be
# auto-selected from the options present (see ifupdown-ng.conf).
# The loopback stanza below is live and safe on any machine. The eth0
# examples are the ADMIN-GUIDE's own -- enable ONE, adapted to your real
# interface name and addresses. Executor-specific options are documented
# in ifupdown-executor(7) and interfaces(5), not enumerated here.
# Source: upstream ifupdown-ng doc/ADMIN-GUIDE.md "Interface
# Configuration" (accessed 2026-09-28;
# https://github.com/ifupdown-ng/ifupdown-ng).
# Real location: /etc/network/interfaces
# ---
# The loopback interface. Always wanted; configure it first.
auto lo
iface lo inet loopback

# --- Example 1: desktop with DHCP (IPv4, and DHCPv6 via dhcpcd) ---
#auto eth0
#iface eth0
